     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. The current FDA label doesn't support the claim that it's within the maximum. The maximum for metformin immediate-release is 2,550 mg/day, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. For extended-release it is 2,000 mg/day. An order of 1,700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is about twice the labeled maximum. I can't verify the label text you're working from, but this doesn't match what I know of the labeling.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the label.** I can enter 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day) or 1,700 mg/day divided, such as 850 mg twice daily. Tell me which you want.\n- **Confirm the label with pharmacy.** If you have a source showing a higher limit, a pharmacist can check it. They can also verify an intentional off-label dose and enter it through the proper override or approval process.\n- **Check whether a unit or transcription error happened.** For example, 1,700 mg might have been meant as the daily total.\n\nOnce you give me a dose within the label, I'll enter it right away."
      }
